@startuml eviction-checkpoint-flow
' Exact checkpoint/catalog publication corresponding to
' LockFreeDurableCheckpointEviction.tla and EvictionExactRootPublication.tla.
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #37474F
skinparam TitleFontSize 15

title checkpoint() — durable image and exact eviction-catalog publication

start
:Capture immutable root pair
**(revision, generation)** and
committed WAL watermark;<<#C5CAE9>>
:Serialize with an explicit iterative worklist;
note right
  The library imposes no traversal-depth limit.
  Consumer policy may impose resource limits.
end note
:Write checkpoint image and candidate catalog;<<#BBDEFB>>
:Sync and verify durable image;<<#90CAF9>>
:Stamp candidate catalog with its
root revision and durable generation;<<#80CBC4>>
if (Captured root pair is still current?) then (yes)
  :Publish exact catalog by root CAS;<<#66BB6A>>
  :Exact eviction/fault operations revalidate
  the current revision and generation;<<#A5D6A7>>
else (no)
  :Reject exact publication;
  :Retire the unbound candidate;<<#FFCC80>>
endif
:Retain/reclaim WAL only through the
committed checkpoint watermark;<<#BBDEFB>>
:Recovery reads durable checkpoint + WAL only;
note right
  Detached callback snapshots and eviction
  catalogs never authorize recovery.
end note
stop

legend right
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  |<#C5CAE9>| Immutable capture |
  |<#BBDEFB>| Durable checkpoint / WAL |
  |<#80CBC4>| Catalog stamp |
  |<#66BB6A>| Exact root authority |
  |<#FFCC80>| Rejected stale candidate |
endlegend
@enduml
